=================PLAN================ (complete, yay)
Make a sudoku checker
* The sudoku
  - Is a nested tuple with opening by applying with the row number and column number
  - (λf. f (λg. g...) (λg. g ...) ... (λg. g ...))
  - with each tuple having 9 elements, the g tuple contains 9 numbers.
  
* Numbers
  - Are really just selectors of 9 elements
  - Easier to control than actual numerals
  
* Thingy
  - AND9: a 9-input AND gate.
  - AND3: a 3-input AND gate.
  - ta: tail function.
  - MARK: mark the bth element of a (the 9-tuple full of F) by turning it into a T
  - MAP: function that applies a function to every tuple of that function.
  - isE: checks if whether the input is E rather than 1-9
  - CCTN: Concatenates the sudoku into a tuple with 81 elements
  - RERCCR: Reorder them to make every column a row (r,c) -> (c,r)
  - REBRC: Reorder them to make every box a row
  - MAP: map every element of the 9-tuple to the function. tuple(map(j, a)) in Python idk
  - VALID_ROW: recursively get the first element of a tuple of 9 elements,
    run that through the mark and then transforming the tuple
    (a,b,c,d,e,f,g,h,i) → (b,c,d,e,f,g,h,i,E)
    repeat until first is E
    this is made for the length of the tuple to not be changing and make the head function also be fixed
    And then apply ALLT to that. oh and the starting 9-tuple that gets marked is (λa.a F F F F F F F F F)
  - VALID_ROWS: check if all rows of a sudoku is valid.
  - CHECKER: Checks if all rows, columns and boxes are all unique. The thing I made.
